// Syncthing ignore rules for C:\CryptoNite-MT5-Bots\
// Apply on EVERY device: Syncthing UI -> Folder -> Edit -> Ignore Patterns
// Editing .stignore file alone is NOT enough — must paste into the UI on each device.
//
// WHAT CHANGED vs old rules:
//   REMOVED from ignore: bot.log, events.log, signal_intake.csv, trade_log*, free_signals.log
//   These are now SYNCED so logs are visible on all devices for troubleshooting.
//   Heartbeat and state.json remain excluded (they were the actual cause of perpetual sync).

// ── RUNTIME FILES (written every 10s -- main cause of perpetual syncing) ──
**/heartbeat.txt
**/heartbeat.sync-conflict-*.txt

// ── STATE FILES (machine-specific, not useful to share) ──
**/state.json
**/signal_bridge.json

// ── TELEGRAM SESSION FILES (machine-specific login -- NEVER share) ──
**/*.session
**/*.session-journal

// ── GIT (rewrites index/objects constantly) ──
.git/

// ── PYTHON CACHE (auto-generated per machine) ──
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd

// ── SYNCTHING CONFLICT COPIES (auto-cleanup) ──
**/*.sync-conflict-*

// ── EDITOR / OS JUNK ──
**/*.tmp
**/*.bak
**/*~
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.swp

// ── BACKUPS (large, already on source machine) ──
**/backups/
